WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.880
Please help us!

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.630
Please, we need your help!

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.830
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.250
Shining bright in my heart

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.540
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.750
I'll roll up my sleeves and get walking

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.960
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.210
(Let's do this right)

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:44.580
Being free can feel so restricting

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.920
After all, it never ends

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.330
This spiral of theoretical values and test results

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.420
Whether I win or lose

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.000
(No matter what I try)

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.670
I work hard to see my dream come true

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.500
(It's not a cheat, it's a life hack)

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.960
I've got the license to take my proper first step

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.250
This is just the beginning

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:08.500
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.880
Shining bright in my heart

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.250
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.830
I take a deep breath before work

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:22.000
Resound, as I reach out towards a whole new world

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.330
My dream is surely in my hands

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.750
An original only I can make

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.460
Open that door and say welcome

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.960
(This is the start)

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.460
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.880
(Let's do this right)

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.750
Iris...

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.080
Iris...

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.460
The worst injury is her torn right arm.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.170
Then there are the burns on her left arm,
and the poison too...

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.540
Please, save Iris!

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.710
I can do it.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:00.960
R-really?!

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.500
But it will cost a great deal.

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:08.830
Hey! You're talking about money
at a time like this?!

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.880
Shut it!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.670
Don't go talking like damn amateurs!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.790
That young lady's serious here!

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.880
If you wanna call yourselves gatherers,
you've gotta be prepared for times like this!

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.330
But...!

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.710
There are two ways I can handle this.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.330
The first would save her life,
but nothing further.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.380
The other would allow her to recover fully.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.130
I'll pay whatever it takes! So please...!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.130
Bring Iris back to how she was!

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.920
Understood!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.630
So, could you...

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.630
I'm Kate.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.750
Ms. Kate, could you go draw water?

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.580
On it!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.580
Lorea, show her the way!

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.830
Ah, yes!

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.420
This way, Ms. Kate!

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.080
Step aside!

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.290
Could you describe the circumstances
of how this happened to her, mister...?

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.750
The name's Andre.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.040
We just found them at the village entrance
and brought them here.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:05.920
But from what they said, they ran into
some sort of nasty bear-like creature.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.920
They said it had four arms,
and even breathed flame, right?

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.170
Yeah.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.170
That would be a monster.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.170
Huh?!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.540
In all likelihood, a hellflame grizzly.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.130
Hellflame...

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.460
Grizzly...

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.500
Here's the water.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.500
Place it down there.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.540
Right!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.960
Well then, I'll start by reattaching her arm.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.880
Please put it in place.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.080
O-okay!

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.170
Alright, that should handle her arm.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.290
I see that first aid was done
on her stomach wound,

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.130
so next up she'll need an antidote.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.130
Hmm...

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.750
She still hasn't regained consciousness.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.920
That takes care of the poison!

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.000
Next up, could you hand me
a stamina recovery potion, Lorea?!

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.170
Er, which one...?

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.250
The expensive one!

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.250
This is a battle against time, here!

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.130
R-right!

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.130
What, you're bringing up price again?!

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.500
You're obsessed with money!

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.380
Shut up!

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.920
Iris only got hurt in the first place

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.420
because you two charged in
all on your own, right?!

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.170
Now's not the time for discussing that!

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.420
What I'm taking issue here is how she's
been weighing a life with money...

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.380
What's the matter with weighing them
against one another?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.880
Gatherers make a living selling the goods
they risk their lives to get ahold of.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.790
We alchemists make a living by
receiving money for our services,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.210
making medicine and artifacts,

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.920
and sometimes saving lives.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.290
They're the same thing...
Weighing the value of life.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.420
But...!

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:04.040
You guys wouldn't accept the idea
of giving the things you gathered

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.830
to someone for free
just to help them out, right?

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.500
We've all got roles to play.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.210
Make sure you keep that in mind.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.830
Now then, little lady...

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.500
Ah, is it rude to go calling you that?

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.790
My name is Sarasa.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.880
Seems we'll just be in the way at this point,
so we'll head out here, Sarasa.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.920
But if there's anything I can do
to help out, just let me know.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.290
See ya!

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.960
Thank you.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.210
Owner...

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.250
Did I go a bit too far there...?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.330
Even if I have to weigh the value of life
and money against one another...

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.250
that doesn't change the fact
that I want to save Ms. Iris!

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:39.880
Owner...

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.170
Next up, we'll fully heal her stomach injury,
which already received first aid!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.170
Right!

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.130
I believe everything should be fine for now.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:06:00.290
She lost a lot of blood, so her face is still pale,
but her breathing has calmed.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.080
Now she just needs to keep drinking
stamina recovery potions, so...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.460
Thank you!

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.790
I really thought that she was done for...

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.080
I'm so glad.
Now I can finally relax too...

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.170
so...

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.420
What's the matter, Owner?!

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.580
Are you alright, Ms. Sarasa?!

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.880
I pushed myself a bit there,
so my nerves just sort of gave out.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.670
Ms. Kate, please feel free to stay here
with Ms. Iris for the time being.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.460
Huh?

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.420
That sounds safer than trying to
take her back to the inn, but still...

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.540
Is it really okay?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.580
Yes, I'd feel more at ease
that way myself, too.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.500
Thanks, Owner!

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.670
Thanks so much for everything today.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.670
Ah, no, I wasn't really able
to do much of note.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.960
That's not true...

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:53.710
Still, was it a bit too much for you, perhaps?

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.830
Honestly, I was surprised.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:59.380
So alchemists deal with
situations like that too, huh?

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.130
That's only natural
when you handle medicines.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:06.790
I did a lot of training, but I'd say that was
my first ever actual experience.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.290
Really?

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.420
But you seemed so calm and composed.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.420
Actually...

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:14.290
It really was a whole lot for me to handle.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:22.540
Still, I sure am glad Ms. Kate
said that she would pay.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.670
I wanted to save her too, after all.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.580
Right.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.960
Those men sure were awful, though!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:32.330
I'm not really familiar with them,
aside from Mr. Andre.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.460
Ms. Kate said they teamed up with them
for the first time today, too.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.920
They didn't know a thing about
how you felt, Ms. Sarasa...

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.710
But well, I just had to say my piece.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.630
If I went and gave out treatment for free,

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.920
my alchemy business could easily fall apart.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:54.630
If Ms. Kate happened to say she couldn't pay,
what would you have done?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.170
That's a difficult question...

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:01.040
I may have gone ahead and saved her anyway.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:06.920
There are times when alchemists
have to act in that manner, though.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.710
In order to save as many people as possible.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.210
Many people...?

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.630
For example, there's a limit to
how many potions you can make,

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.000
and ingredients aren't limitless either.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.750
That's why there needs to be
an exchange of money,

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.830
and it's the reason for the relationship
between alchemists and gatherers.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:27.500
That system is meant to keep things equal.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:31.380
So ignoring that to save a single life now

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:34.210
could lead to even more lives
being lost in the end.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:37.500
I want alchemy to help protect everyone,

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:42.080
and that's why I need to be strict...
when it comes to the value of life.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.790
I can definitely understand that.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.290
Thank you for teaching me properly.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.670
Right back at you, Lorea.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.170
Thank you for listening.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.540
Ka...te...

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.000
Iris!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.250
Thank goodness...

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:22.710
Ms. Owner, my deepest apologies
for imposing on you so.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.790
I, Iris Lotze, offer you my heartfelt
gratitude for saving my life.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.130
Don't worry about it.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.040
I couldn't exactly just leave you be.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.170
Besides, it isn't as if I did it free of charge.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:37.670
Speaking of which,
how much shall the fee be...?

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:43.040
Well, between the treatment and potions,
it should be around...

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.380
Huh?!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.710
Th-that much...?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.210
Of course, I'm not asking you
to pay that all at once.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:56.880
I have no intention of pushing you on the matter,
so please don't worry so much.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.670
Between the two of us, I'm sure we'll be fine!

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:02.290
Let's work hard to pay it off together!

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.290
Kate!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.460
Also, I have a question
I'd like to ask the two of you.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.500
Wh-what might that be?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.630
It's about the monster that attacked you...

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.630
The hellflame grizzly.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.880
Around where did you encounter it?

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:20.000
It wasn't all that far off, was it?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:25.330
Right. I ran here like a madwoman,
but it didn't take all that long.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.710
That sounds pretty close.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.630
It won't come here to the village, will it?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.250
I'm not so sure...

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.000
Huh?!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.830
Unlike normal animals, there are
all sorts of monsters out there.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.750
We can't go letting our guards down.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.130
Alright, I guess it's time to
go gather up some ingredients.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:45.170
Huh?!

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:47.710
Ah, hey, don't go treating it
so lightly there, Owner!

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.750
That's right!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.380
You'll end up being
the one injured at this rate!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:55.250
Hmm, I don't think it's anything
worth worrying that much over...

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.460
Ms. Owner!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:01.000
Are you perhaps... terribly strong?

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.710
Well I've had sword training,

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:07.790
so I don't think a single hellflame grizzly
would be any real trouble.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.170
Even so!

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.500
I cannot allow you to venture forth
on your own, Ms. Owner!

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.750
Allow me to accompany you,
as an official gatherer!

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.170
Huh?! But you only just recovered, Ms. Iris!

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.830
I'll come along too.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:25.290
I want to do at least a little something
to repay you, just like Iris.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:30.580
Well, it's true that I'd need people
to help carry the ingredients...

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.000
Then should I reach out to
Mr. Andre's group too?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.960
I'm sure they'd prove helpful.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.210
This is turning into quite a big party...

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:42.960
Still, I suppose it will be
my first time exploring the area.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:46.670
Indeed! If you treat monsters lightly,
you'll suffer a terrible fate!

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.000
That's seriously convincing!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:56.130
Well then, let's all go on a bear hunt together!

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.540
Yeah!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.130
Hup...

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.460
I can't believe it...!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.750
She didn't need us at all, huh?

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:28.630
I thought for sure that you'd
take it down with your sword.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.500
I brought it along to be on the safe side,

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.790
but I'm able to gather more ingredients
by not cutting it down.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.130
And so, time to get dissecting!

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.880
Ooh...

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.500
That's a nice flame sac.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:47.290
It's so soft and slick,
so it must be pretty high quality!

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.580
She certainly is skilled.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.380
Yes, we truly are observing a pro at work!

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:56.500
I gotta reach all the way in while
taking care not to damage the stomach...

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.790
Ah, there it is!

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:01.960
A nice, fresh liver!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.000
Now then, last up are the eyeballs...

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:09.460
Hmm?

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.170
Oh no...

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.380
A hellflame grizzly frenzy?

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.250
Yes, there's a very high risk of that.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.130
Huh?! But why?!

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:25.250
When there's a shortage of the flame stones
hellflame grizzlies primarily eat,

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.920
they lose control and start running wild.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.630
These red eyeballs are a sign of that.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.000
Once they start rampaging,

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.960
they'll attack nearby towns and
villages indiscriminately.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.380
At best they would only number
around ten or so,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.670
but at worst,
it could be over a hundred.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.880
I can't believe it...!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:50.170
They should be here tomorrow at the soonest,
and within six days at the latest.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:53.170
In that case, we need to contact
the lord of the land...

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:57.170
Ah, but even if we do that,
there's no telling if help will arrive in time!

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.080
Pull yourself together, Mayor.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.710
Isn't there anything we can do, Sarasa?

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.920
I'll help out as much as I can, but...

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:07.210
Is there anyone here in the village
who can fight?

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:09.790
Just the hunter, Jasper.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.500
And our village doesn't have
the money to hire anyone else.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.210
I shall lend my assistance!

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.330
And I'll help however I can too.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.330
That goes for us too, of course.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.290
I'll also try to reach out
to some other gatherers.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.000
Even so, we just won't have enough people
to protect the whole village...

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.460
Yes, but there's a way to handle this!

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:29.380
Huh?!

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.080
Let's all work together to overcome this!

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.790
If we put all our wits together,
I'm sure we can make it through somehow.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.040
Probably...

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.880
We're gonna be attacked by monsters?

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:47.170
And you're saying we've gotta
do something about it?

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.170
Yes.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:49.920
What'll we do...?

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.710
Sorry, Sarasa.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.460
Most of the gatherers around ran away.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.380
Huh?!

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:58.080
Apparently those two that were in our party

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.460
went around talking about
how frightening hellflame grizzlies are.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.830
Honestly, this is going to be tough.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:07.040
So, just where should we start?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.000
Huh?!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.630
Yeah! It's not like we'd have anywhere
to go if we ran for it anyway!

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:15.040
So we've got no choice
but to protect our village ourselves!

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.920
Isn't that right, everybody?!

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.330
Darn straight!

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.330
Well then, please start by building a fence!

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.080
Yeah!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:33.630
We'll use the fence to guide the hellflame
grizzlies from the forest to a single spot,

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.500
and take them down all at once.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:42.130
And we'll leave the flame stones they eat
in the center as bait, to better draw them in.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:46.130
Those of you who can't fight, please help with
keeping watch and herding the monsters.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.380
Leave it to us.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.540
We'll stir those monsters up properly.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.040
My hubby's a hunter, so he can fight too!

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:59.420
And he can head out into the forest and
let us know when the monsters are coming!

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.040
The name's Jasper.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.880
I've at least got a good set of eyes
and sense of smell, so you can count on me!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.960
Right, that's a big help!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.540
Thank you, Mr. Andre.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.250
Hmm? What for?

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:24.830
For staying here in the village, rather than
running away like the other gatherers.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.500
Of course.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.920
I mean, we've worked out of
this village for forever.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.500
Yup, that's right.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:35.170
We won't go running away
while you folks are in trouble.

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:39.170
That goes extra when kids like you
are working so hard.

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:43.960
Ah, I'm fifteen, so I'm technically an adult!

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.290
Preparations are going smoothly.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.130
It seems like we'll pull through, doesn't it?

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.380
I certainly hope so.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.000
You sure did make a lot.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.750
Yeah, because I've been making them
for the last three days straight.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:19.250
Is the shop going to be alright,
with you making this many?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.170
Since we're ignoring profits here,
we're way in the red.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:25.460
To be honest, if I don't get ahold of
ingredients from the hellflame grizzlies,

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.710
things will be looking pretty bad.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:31.420
Still, I've got to give my all
for everyone in the village!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:34.670
After all, I love this place...

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:36.880
Ms. Sarasa...

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.250
What's that?

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:41.670
That's the signal that they've started moving!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.130
Calm yourselves!

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.080
Don't panic! Just take your positions!

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:53.330
Jasper!

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.380
There are over twenty of them!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:58.080
They're not moving fast, but they're
coming out of the forest, sure enough.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:12.750
I only still live thanks to
the owner's miraculous power.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.080
That cannot happen again, though!

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.670
I shall never again waste this life of mine!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.830
Go ahead and take shelter
on the second floor, Lorea.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.460
And if anything happens, blow that whistle!

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.960
Got it! Be careful, Ms. Sarasa!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.500
Right, thanks!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.540
Ms. Sarasa...

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.880
Oh, come on...

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:43.420
They're seriously that huge?

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.830
Don't falter! Stick to the plan!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.000
Force bullet!

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.000
Sarasa!

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.500
Sorry I'm late.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.000
There's nothing to worry about.
We're guiding the monsters properly.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.290
We should be plenty capable of
taking them down if we work together!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.880
You heard her!
Let's protect the village, everyone!

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:33.580
The sunlight gently streams in through my window

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.750
Yeah!

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:39.330
Whispering that it's time to get up

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.750
Let's do this!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:45.380
Bringing my anticipation and a bit of courage with me

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:50.960
I set off to look for a tiny bit of growth

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:57.330
Peering lightly through the door opened for the first time

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.080
Hey, don't head that way!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.830
Yeah! Over here! Come on!

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:04.830
My heart is pounding, alongside plenty of smiles

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:06.420
Curses!

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:12.710
Squeezing in plenty of new encounters

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:08.920
Use this!

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:17.630
Each time we mingle, a harmony is born

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:24.500
I want to believe in every possibility

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.750
Are you okay, Ms. Iris?

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.170
Ms. Owner...

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.790
I'm in your debt.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:32.960
Just like I believe this sky will be clear again tomorrow

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.000
Things are looking good.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.250
It feels like we're going to manage
somehow, doesn't it, Sarasa?!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.210
Yeah.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.080
Th-that thing's huge!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:43.040
We've got a boss class one here!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.790
We'll all have to take it on together!

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.750
Even then, I'm not sure we can win...!

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.540
Ms. Owner!

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.750
Water ball!

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:02.130
Ms. Owner!

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:33.880
Splendid work, Ms. Owner!

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:37.000
I'm seriously at a loss for words.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:44.880
If I recall correctly,
that whistle sound means...

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:45.960
Lorea!

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:47.710
Ms. Owner!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:50.330
Lorea!

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:08.830
Lorea!

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:10.710
Ms. Sarasa!

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:12.670
Lorea!

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:17.580
And I'll always be
on your side too, Ms. Sarasa!

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:20.830
If you bears mean to do Lorea harm...

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:22.420
I'll slaughter you!

00:22:29.380 --> 00:22:30.630
Ms. Sarasa?!

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:44.750
Are you alright, Lorea?

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:47.460
Yes, I'm fine...

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:49.170
Thank goodness!

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:55.830
We did it! We won!

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:06.000
Looks like it's over.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:07.000
Ms. Sarasa!

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.000
Hey... Lorea?

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.670
I'm glad you're okay!

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:12.250
So very glad!

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:14.000
You're making too big a deal about it.

00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:16.080
B-but...

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:19.290
This much was child's play for me!

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.420
No problem at all!

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:24.500
Eh? Eh?

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.000
M-Ms. Sarasa!

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:30.330
Hold on, Ms. Sarasa!

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:34.540
Oh no! Ms. Sarasa!

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Iris's Treatment:</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Potions Supplied (Current Price):</b>
